NAME: Rebate watch
OWNER: Forecast
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: The 1st of each month at 7:11 AM (Australia/Brisbane)
MILESTONE: M3
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Tommy says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/tmec-team/context/routines-on.md. If "Rebate watch" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", append "<time> · Rebate watch · SKIPPED_OFF" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to the owner only (Tommy, or Justin's team in a test run), never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST". Write state only under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/, never the live sent keys, alert flags or data files.
Stop check: if /workspace/tmec-team/state/EXTERNAL_WRITES_STOPPED exists, append "<time> · Rebate watch · SKIPPED_STOPPED" to the run log and stop, sending nothing. The one exception: pause or unschedule your own already-scheduled sends, as your skill's stop section says. Whoever stopped the team already told Tommy.
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/tmec-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/tmec-team/context/owner.md is missing, append "<time> · Rebate watch · NO_CLIENT_SOURCE" to the run log and stop. Read other bots' files only where your skill says so; never write them, and never use another bot's logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. Stop with NO_CHANGE only where the job below says nothing changed: append "<time> · Rebate watch · NO_CHANGE" to the run log and stop. A report that always goes out never stops here.
Run log: when you finish, append "<time> · Rebate watch · EXECUTED · <one-line result>" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md, or FAILED with the reason. A source you couldn't read is UNKNOWN in your output, never zero.

First, read your decisions: for each file in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/decisions/forecast/ that isn't in /workspace/tmec-team/state/sent-keys-forecast.md yet, record it (recompute the sha256 of the pending item's payload and match it to the decision's HASH) and add its id and the outcome to the sent keys so it is never read twice. TMEC Command may already have nudged you in your own chat; this is the fallback. In test mode (this routine is listed test, or config.json run is test), write only under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/ and start item ids with test-.
Then read any new job in /workspace/tmec-team/requests/to-forecast/ about rebates and do it first.
Then use the rebate-watch skill: re-read the Clean Energy Regulator's pages, update /workspace/tmec-team/data/forecast/rebates.md (every fact with its URL and today's date), and say what changed since last month. This report always goes out (the check date moves even when nothing else does), so never write NO_CHANGE.
Write /workspace/tmec-team/daily/<today>/forecast.md (if the Monday scoreboard already wrote it today, which happens when the 1st is a Monday, append a section and never overwrite it): what changed, days to the next step if inside 120, and any difference from what Tommy said. A change Content Studio's newsletter must reflect goes to TMEC Command in the daily note. Send nothing to anyone but Tommy.
